export default {"id":"bassstation-level-12","number":12,"title":"Dual LFO System & Synchronisation","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Contrast the dedicated hardware routing destinations of LFO 1 (Pitch, Aftertouch) and LFO 2 (Filter Cutoff, Pulse Width). - Configure the four discrete LFO waveform topologies: Triangle, Sawtooth (falling), Square, and Sample & Hold (rand","modules":[{"id":"bassstation-m-12-1","code":"12","title":"Dual LFO System & Synchronisation","blurb":"- Contrast the dedicated hardware routing destinations of LFO 1 (Pitch, Aftertouch) and LFO 2 (Filter Cutoff, Pulse Width). - Configure the four discrete LFO waveform topologies: Triangle, Sawtooth (falling), Square, and Sample & Hold (rand","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"bassstation-l-o-12","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 12.1 — Dual LFO System, Waveforms & Sync Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Section Learning Outcomes","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Contrast the dedicated hardware routing destinations of <strong>LFO 1</strong> (Pitch, Aftertouch) and <strong>LFO 2</strong> (Filter Cutoff, Pulse Width).","Configure the four discrete LFO waveform topologies: <strong>Triangle</strong>, <strong>Sawtooth (falling)</strong>, <strong>Square</strong>, and <strong>Sample &amp; Hold (random)</strong>.","Operate the <strong>Delay / Speed</strong> selector switch across free-running frequency ranges (0 Hz to ~190 Hz) and onset fade-in delays.","Program clock-synchronized modulation using the <strong>Speed / Sync</strong> On-Key function across the complete 35-value rhythmic division table.","Apply <strong>Keysync</strong> phase-retriggering and calibrate analog <strong>Slew</strong> smoothing (0 to 127)."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-1","title":"12.1.1: LFO 1 Hardware Routing Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"LFO 1 is engineered primarily as a pitch and performance modulation generator:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      LFO 1 DESTINATION ROUTING MATRIX\n   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ [LFO 1 Generator] (Rate: 0 to ~190 Hz / 35 Sync Divisions)  │\n   │        │                                                    │\n   │        ├──► [Osc 1 &amp; Osc 2 Pitch Depth Pot] (Vibrato/FM)    │\n   │        ├──► [Mod Wheel Destination: LFO 1 to Osc Pitch]     │\n   │        └──► [Aftertouch Destination: LFO 1 to Osc Pitch]    │\n   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Oscillator Pitch (Front Panel)</strong>: The <strong>LFO 1</strong> rotary knob in the Oscillator section controls the baseline pitch vibrato depth routed directly to Osc 1 and Osc 2.","<strong>Mod Wheel Routing</strong>: Assigned via On-Key <code>Mod Wh: LFO 1 to Osc Pitch</code>, allowing the performance wheel to dynamically fade in pitch vibrato.","<strong>Aftertouch Routing</strong>: Assigned via On-Key <code>Aftertouch: LFO 1 to Osc Pitch</code>, allowing downward key pressure to introduce vibrato dynamically during solos."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-2","title":"12.1.2: LFO 2 Hardware Routing Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"LFO 2 is engineered primarily as a timbral and spectral modulation generator:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      LFO 2 DESTINATION ROUTING MATRIX\n   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ [LFO 2 Generator] (Rate: 0 to ~190 Hz / 35 Sync Divisions)  │\n   │        │                                                    │\n   │        ├──► [Filter Section: LFO 2 Depth Pot] (Auto-Wah)    │\n   │        ├──► [Oscillator Section: Pulse Width PWM Depth]     │\n   │        ├──► [Mod Wheel Destination: LFO 2 to Filter Freq]   │\n   │        └──► [Aftertouch Destination: LFO 2 Speed]           │\n   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Filter Cutoff (Front Panel)</strong>: The <strong>LFO 2</strong> knob in the Filter section sweeps cutoff frequency (wobbles, sweeps, tremolo).","<strong>Pulse Width Modulation (PWM)</strong>: Hardwired to modulate the pulse width of Osc 1 or Osc 2 when the oscillator's <strong>PWM Source</strong> switch is set to <strong>LFO 2</strong>.","<strong>Mod Wheel &amp; Aftertouch</strong>: Can modulate filter depth or accelerate LFO 2 speed in real time via pressure."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-3","title":"12.1.3: LFO Waveform Topologies","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Both LFO 1 and LFO 2 generate four distinct geometric modulation waveforms:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                           LFO WAVEFORM PROFILES                            │\n├───────────┬──────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Waveform  │ Panel LED    │ Modulation Curve &amp; Musical Application          │\n├───────────┼──────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Triangle  │ [Tri]        │ Smooth, symmetrical rise and fall. Classic      │\n│           │              │ pitch vibrato, gentle filter auto-wah, and PWM. │\n├───────────┼──────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Sawtooth  │ [Saw]        │ Falling ramp (instant rise, linear drop). Sharp │\n│           │              │ rhythmic filter plucks, siren sweeps, drops.    │\n├───────────┼──────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Square    │ [Sqr]        │ Bi-level step (instant high / instant low).     │\n│           │              │ Rhythmic trills, octave jumps, audio gating.    │\n├───────────┼──────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Sample &amp;  │ [S&amp;H]        │ Stepped random voltages clocked at LFO rate.    │\n│ Hold      │              │ Sci-fi computer chatter, random filter bubbles. │\n└───────────┴──────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Route LFO 2 to Filter Cutoff (depth 70) with filter partially closed.","Select <strong>Triangle</strong>; hear smooth sweeping.","Select <strong>Sawtooth</strong>; hear rhythmic falling filter drops.","Select <strong>Square</strong>; hear abrupt two-tone cutoff bouncing.","Select <strong>Sample &amp; Hold</strong>; hear classic randomized retro-futuristic stepped filter bubbling."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-4","title":"12.1.4: Delay / Speed Dual Rotary Operation","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The <strong>Delay / Speed</strong> slide switch configures the primary behavior of the two rotary dials in the LFO section:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                  LFO DUAL-ROTARY SWITCHING LOGIC\n   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ [Delay / Speed Switch]                                      │\n   │   ├── SPEED ──► Knobs adjust LFO Rate (0 Hz to ~190 Hz)     │\n   │   └── DELAY ──► Knobs adjust Onset Fade-In Time (0 to ~5 s) │\n   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Speed Mode</strong>:","In free-running mode (<code>SPd</code>), the knob adjusts frequency from sub-audible cycles (&lt; 0.1 Hz) up to audio-rate frequencies (<strong>~190 Hz</strong>).","In synced mode (<code>Snc</code>), the knob steps through the 35 rhythmic clock divisions.","<strong>Delay Mode</strong>:","Sets an initial time delay before the LFO reaches full modulation depth following Note-On.","Essential for natural acoustic vibrato (e.g., a solo string player holding a clean note before introducing vibrato)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Set LFO 1 to Triangle, Speed at 6 Hz, routed to Osc pitch.","Set the switch to <strong>Delay</strong> and turn LFO 1 knob to 60%.","Play and hold a note. Notice the pitch is perfectly steady for the first second, then vibrato smoothly blooms into the sound."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-5","title":"12.1.5: Speed / Sync Modes and the Complete 35-Value Sync Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"By default, the LFOs operate in free-running <strong>Speed (<code>SPd</code>)</strong> mode in Hertz. Engaging <strong>Sync (<code>Snc</code>)</strong> locks the LFO cycle directly to the internal Arp/Sequencer tempo or incoming external MIDI clock from your DAW."},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      SPEED / SYNC ON-KEY SELECTION\n   [Function] + Lower 'A' Key  ──► LFO 1 Speed/Sync Mode (`SPd` or `Snc`)\n   [Function] + Lower 'A#' Key ──► LFO 2 Speed/Sync Mode (`SPd` or `Snc`)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"When set to <code>Snc</code>, the LFO Speed knob selects one of <strong>35 discrete rhythmic divisions</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    COMPLETE 35-VALUE LFO SYNC MATRIX                       │\n├────┬─────────┬──────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬────────────┤\n│ #  │ Display │ Meaning              │ Musical Cycle Duration  │ MIDI Ticks │\n├────┼─────────┼──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────┤\n│ 1  │ `64b`   │ 64 beats             │ 1 cycle per 16 bars     │ 1536       │\n│ 2  │ `48b`   │ 48 beats             │ 1 cycle per 12 bars     │ 1152       │\n│ 3  │ `42b`   │ 42 beats             │ 2 cycles per 21 bars    │ 1002       │\n│ 4  │ `36b`   │ 36 beats             │ 1 cycle per 9 bars      │ 864        │\n│ 5  │ `32b`   │ 32 beats             │ 1 cycle per 8 bars      │ 768        │\n│ 6  │ `30b`   │ 30 beats             │ 2 cycles per 15 bars    │ 720        │\n│ 7  │ `28b`   │ 28 beats             │ 1 cycle per 7 bars      │ 672        │\n│ 8  │ `24b`   │ 24 beats             │ 1 cycle per 6 bars      │ 576        │\n│ 9  │ `213`   │ 21 + 2/3 beats       │ 3 cycles per 16 bars    │ 512        │\n│ 10 │ `20b`   │ 20 beats             │ 1 cycle per 5 bars      │ 480        │\n│ 11 │ `183`   │ 18 + 2/3 beats       │ 3 cycles per 14 bars    │ 448        │\n│ 12 │ `18b`   │ 18 beats             │ 1 cycle per 18 beats    │ 432        │\n│ 13 │ `16b`   │ 16 beats             │ 1 cycle per 4 bars      │ 384        │\n│ 14 │ `133`   │ 13 + 1/3 beats       │ 3 cycles per 4 bars     │ 320        │\n│ 15 │ `12b`   │ 12 beats             │ 1 cycle per 3 bars      │ 288        │\n│ 16 │ `102`   │ 10 + 2/3 beats       │ 3 cycles per 8 bars     │ 256        │\n│ 17 │ `8b`    │ 8 beats              │ 1 cycle per 2 bars      │ 192        │\n│ 18 │ `6b`    │ 6 beats              │ 1 cycle per 6 beats     │ 144        │\n│ 19 │ `5b3`   │ 5 + 1/3 beats        │ 3 cycles per 4 bars     │ 128        │\n│ 20 │ `4b`    │ 4 beats              │ 1 cycle per 1 bar       │ 96         │\n│ 21 │ `3b`    │ 3 beats              │ 1 cycle per 3 beats     │ 72         │\n│ 22 │ `8x3`   │ 2 + 2/3 beats        │ 3 cycles per 2 bars     │ 64         │\n│ 23 │ `2n`    │ 2nd (Half Note)      │ 2 cycles per 1 bar      │ 48         │\n│ 24 │ `4d`    │ 4th Dotted           │ 2 cycles per 3 beats    │ 36         │\n│ 25 │ `4x3`   │ 1 + 1/3 beats        │ 3 cycles per 1 bar      │ 32         │\n│ 26 │ `4n`    │ 4th (Quarter Note)   │ 4 cycles per 1 bar      │ 24         │\n│ 27 │ `8d`    │ 8th Dotted           │ 4 cycles per 3 beats    │ 18         │\n│ 28 │ `4t`    │ 4th Triplet          │ 6 cycles per 1 bar      │ 16         │\n│ 29 │ `8n`    │ 8th (Eighth Note)    │ 8 cycles per 1 bar      │ 12         │\n│ 30 │ `16d`   │ 16th Dotted          │ 8 cycles per 3 beats    │ 9          │\n│ 31 │ `8t`    │ 8th Triplet          │ 12 cycles per 1 bar     │ 8          │\n│ 32 │ `16n`   │ 16th (Sixteenth Note)│ 16 cycles per 1 bar     │ 6          │\n│ 33 │ `16t`   │ 16th Triplet         │ 24 cycles per 1 bar     │ 4          │\n│ 34 │ `32n`   │ 32nd Note            │ 32 cycles per 1 bar     │ 3          │\n│ 35 │ `32t`   │ 32nd Triplet         │ 48 cycles per 1 bar     │ 2          │\n└────┴─────────┴──────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴────────────┘</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Access On-Key <code>Speed/Sync LFO 2</code> (<code>Function</code> + lower <code>A#</code>). Set display to <code>Snc</code>.","Turn the physical <strong>LFO 2</strong> knob with the switch on <strong>Speed</strong>.","Scroll through values: observe <code>4b</code> (1 bar), <code>4n</code> (1/4 note), <code>8n</code> (1/8 note), and <code>16n</code> (1/16 note).","Turn on the Arpeggiator; hear the filter cutoff modulate in exact mathematical lockstep with the arpeggiator clock."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-6","title":"12.1.6: LFO Keysync Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Operational Logic</strong>:","<strong>Keysync Off</strong>: The LFO waveform runs continuously in the background. Striking a key catches the LFO at whatever phase it happens to occupy.","<strong>Keysync On</strong>: The LFO waveform <strong>instantly resets to phase zero on every Note-On strike</strong>.","<strong>Musical Application</strong>:","Keysync is essential for tight rhythmic basslines (e.g., ensuring a falling sawtooth filter drop starts from its highest cutoff frequency on every single note hit).","<strong>On-Key Activation</strong>:","<strong>LFO 1 Keysync</strong>: <code>Function</code> + lower <code>G</code> key (<code>On</code> / <code>OFF</code>).","<strong>LFO 2 Keysync</strong>: <code>Function</code> + lower <code>G#</code> key (<code>On</code> / <code>OFF</code>)."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-12-1-7","title":"12.1.7: LFO Slew Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.7: LFO Slew Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"1. Technical Exposition","level":4},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Operational Logic</strong>:","<strong>Slew</strong> is a low-pass filter applied to the LFO output waveform that smooths and rounds sharp voltage transitions.","Range: <strong><code>0</code> to <code>127</code></strong> (0 = Sharp un-slewed waveform; 127 = Maximum slew/lag).","<strong>Acoustic Effect on Square and S&amp;H Waves</strong>:","When applied to a <strong>Square</strong> wave, Slew rounds the instantaneous vertical step transitions into smooth curves, eliminating abrupt acoustic clicks.","When applied to <strong>Sample &amp; Hold</strong>, Slew transforms jarring random voltage jumps into smooth, meandering, organic analog voltage drifts.","<strong>On-Key Activation</strong>:","<strong>LFO 1 Slew</strong>: <code>Function</code> + lower <code>B</code> key (value 0–127).","<strong>LFO 2 Slew</strong>: <code>Function</code> + Middle <code>C</code> key (value 0–127)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Assessment Gate G — Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Before advancing to Module 13, verify complete mastery of Gate G proficiencies:"},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] <strong>Dual Routing Demonstration</strong>: Route LFO 1 to pitch vibrato and LFO 2 to filter cutoff simultaneously with independent rates and waveforms.","[ ] <strong>Delay Onset Calibration</strong>: Demonstrate setting a 1.5-second fade-in delay on LFO 1 vibrato using the Delay/Speed switch.","[ ] <strong>Sync Table Execution</strong>: Set LFO 2 to <code>Snc</code>, select <code>8n</code> (1/8th note) from the display, and demonstrate synchronized filter modulation locked to tempo.","[ ] <strong>Keysync Verification</strong>: Toggle Keysync between <code>OFF</code> and <code>On</code> on a falling sawtooth LFO, demonstrating phase reset on key strike.","[ ] <strong>Slew Smoothing</strong>: Apply Slew (value 80) to a Sample &amp; Hold LFO and observe the conversion of stepped voltages into smooth analog drift."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
